# A permanent phased out "until [a permanent] leaves the battlefield" phases in immediately after that permanent leaves
# (CR 610.4), partway through the resolution that made it leave (CR 608.2), not once the resolution is over. Bot2's
# Oubliette has phased out Bot2's own Sazh's Chocobo ("Landfall - Whenever a land you control enters, put a +1/+1 counter
# on this creature"), the only creature to target. Bot1's Assassin's Trophy destroys the Oubliette: the Chocobo phases in
# at once, tapped (Oubliette's "Tap that creature as it phases in this way"), before the Trophy's next instruction has Bot2
# search for a basic land and put it onto the battlefield, so the Chocobo sees the Forest enter and gets its counter.
# Had it phased in only after the resolution, the Forest would have entered while it was treated as though it did not
# exist (CR 702.26b), and nothing would have triggered.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Assassin's Trophy
Forest
Swamp x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Sazh's Chocobo
Black Lotus
Oubliette
Island
